[font_size=24][b]Guided Voxel Remesh[/b][/font_size]

Guided Voxel Remesh is an experimental GDScript-only remesher available from the modelling tool shelf.

[font_size=18][b]Whole-object workflow[/b][/font_size]

[ol type=1]
Select an unlocked mesh object.
Open [b]Guided Voxel Remesh[/b].
Set [b]Region[/b] to [b]Whole Object[/b].
Set the voxel resolution and smoothing options.
Optionally choose a guide type and use [b]Draw Guide[/b] to drag a stroke across the surface.
Keep [b]Create Duplicate[/b] selected for the first attempt, then press [b]Remesh[/b].
[/ol]

[font_size=18][b]Selected-face workflow[/b][/font_size]

[ol type=1]
Apply the object's modifier stack. Selected-face remeshing requires the visible face indices to match the stored mesh topology.
Enter Face mode and select the area that should be remeshed.
Open [b]Guided Voxel Remesh[/b] and set [b]Region[/b] to [b]Selected Faces[/b].
Set [b]Boundary Padding[/b]. Two rings is the recommended starting value.
Choose a local resolution. The voxel grid is calculated from the padded selection rather than the whole object, so thin features receive substantially more detail.
Use [b]Create Duplicate[/b] for the first attempt and press [b]Remesh[/b].
[/ol]

Selected-face remeshing extracts the selected faces plus the padding rings, builds a temporary closed voxel shell, keeps the remeshed outer surface, preserves the original padded boundary, and stitches the new surface back into the untouched mesh. The operation refuses to commit a result that creates a non-manifold edge or an additional open boundary.

The operation runs through [code]WorkerThreadPool[/code], reports progress, supports cancellation, and creates one undoable document action when complete.

[font_size=18][b]Guide types[/b][/font_size]

[ul]
[b]Flow[/b] biases vertex relaxation along the stroke and encourages nearby edge rows to follow its direction.
[b]Preserve Shape[/b] reduces smoothing around the stroke and increases projection back to the source surface.
[b]Density[/b] locally subdivides the generated surface around the stroke.
[/ul]

Guide radius and strength apply when a new guide is drawn. Guides are temporary editing data and are not saved in the model document.

[font_size=18][b]Limitations[/b][/font_size]

[ul]
The generated surface is mostly quad-based, but density transitions and preserved-boundary stitching can contain triangles or n-gons.
Selected-face remeshing cannot currently touch an existing open mesh boundary.
Disconnected or branching face selections can fail boundary matching. Select one connected surface region at a time when possible.
Selected-face remeshing requires the modifier stack to be applied first.
It does not create deliberate animation loops comparable to manual retopology or ZRemesher.
Thin details and narrow gaps can close when the voxel resolution is too low.
UVs, seams, creases, loose edges, and custom normals are discarded from the remeshed result.
Open, intersecting, and non-manifold whole-object inputs are accepted, but the voxel result can alter those regions substantially.
Resolution supports values from 12 through 256. Higher resolutions increase processing time and memory use quickly.
The completion message reports the effective resolution. Extremely large voxel grids may be reduced to the safety limit.
[/ul]
